@{
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
    ViewBag.Title = "Part10 - Multiple Language – Globalization";
}

<div class="col-sm-12">
    <p>
        Following previous tutorials, we understood about how to use Fanex.Grid and render technique. In this post, i will introduce to you how we can handle multiple languages in Fanex.Grid.
    </p>
    <p>
        First off all, we need to include all language files install from package http://nuget.nexcel.vn/packages/Fanex.Grid/
    </p>
    <p>
        then refer to all file on “Language” directory.
    </p>
    <p>
        Second, we just need to add property ‘language’, default value is ‘en-US’ if you don’t specific this property, other language can be 'zh-TW', ‘js-JP’, ‘zh-CN’, ‘zh-TW’, ‘vi-VN’, ‘ko-KR’. Seeing example below:
    </p>

    <pre class="brush: javascript">
        var gridOptions =
        {
            ...
            bodyRows: generateData(15000),
            gridExpandHeight: 150,
            numberOfFrozenColumn: 2,
            showPager: true,
            pagerOption: {     
                itemsPerPage: 100,
                currentPage: 0,
                itemsPerPageArray: [50, 100, 500],
                showDetail: true
            },
            language: 'zh-TW'
        };
    </pre>

    <p>And, the result is</p>

    <img width="100%" src="~/Content/Images/Part10-Multiple-Language.png" />
</div>

